Short:        AGA graphics and Bob engine fixes for AMOS Pro
Author:       HWARF (Jerome)
Uploader:     amethist rumor786 passinbox com (Jerome)
Type:         dev/amos
Version:      0.14.1
Requires:     AMOS Professional, AGA chipset, 68020+
Architecture: m68k-amigaos
Distribution: Aminet

Description:
  DRAFT - NOT FOR UPLOAD. Final library and validation pending.

  AMOSPro AGA Extension is an unofficial graphics extension for
  AMOS Professional on AGA Amiga computers and AGA-enabled WinUAE.
  Version 0.14.1 focuses on stability of the software Bob engine
  and existing AGA graphics. No new commands are planned.
  100 commands/functions, 203 AP20 entries, MC68020 minimum.

  Fixes implemented in the P2d-L2 test candidate:
    - Aga Iff Load acquires Safe before bitmap writes; returns
      0 without drawing if Safe is unavailable.
    - Aga Back Fill acquires Safe with up to three WaitTOF
      retries; no drawing if Safe remains unavailable.
    - First B8 Bob binding can acquire an available Safe reply
      after Swap; READY/DIRTY and Swap contracts unchanged.
    - Source provenance and regression tooling synchronization.

  Validation to date (24 Nov 2026, not final):
    - Native Gate A: 172 writer cases and 10 Bob suites passed.
    - Focused SafePort Runtime and Compiler PASS reported.
    - P2 ALL IN ONE Runtime: 240 samples, 252 successful swaps,
      120 refusals recovered. Compiler not retested on L2.
    - EDGE SAFE with pre-VBL: 240/240, zero refusals, Runtime.
    - RPG V9 with pre-VBL: 250 frames, 2 retries, Runtime.
    - Full post-delivery CI and resource checks remain open.
      Physical AGA hardware not tested.
    - Final PASS does not mean zero initial Swap refusals.

  Installation:
    Back up the existing AMOS library and configuration.
    Install AMOSPro_AGA.Lib in APSystem, keep the existing
    extension slot, save configuration and restart AMOS.
    Import ASCII examples via Project / Merge ASCII.

  Only the five C2P commands require c2p.library v1.9 in LIBS:.
    https://aminet.net/package/dev/misc/c2plib
  Aga Iff To Chunky and Bob functions do not require it.

  Current test candidate (not final release identity):
    M19 P2d-L2, 136332 bytes, SHA256:
    b2811e56c12be23697f0bb3c60dbf67f01bdecae0cfb23a787e2d349070f44a1
    Internal ID: "$VER: AMOSPro_AGA M19 P2d-L2".
    Update identity and validation before upload.

  Hardware AGA Sprites are not included in this version.
  Documentation and sources:
    https://github.com/anthea176/AMOSPro-AGA-Extension

